    <mytitle|Setting and definition>

    \;

    <math|\<cal-M\>=\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|L>=<around|(|\<bbb-R\>/L*\<bbb-Z\>|)><rsup|d>>
    or <math|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>>;<space|1em><math|\<cal-S\><around|(|\<cal-M\>|)>>
    smooth, resp. Schwartz, functions;<space|1em><math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around|(|\<cal-M\>|)>>
    with the cylinder (<math|=> Borel) <math|\<sigma\>>-algebra.

    <\equation*>
      A\<assign\>m<rsup|2>-\<Delta\>,<space|2em>C\<assign\>A<rsup|-1>,<space|2em>m\<gtr\>0.
    </equation*>

    <math|A>, <math|C> are continuous bijections of
    <math|\<cal-S\><around|(|\<cal-M\>|)>> (Fourier multipliers
    <math|<around|(|<around|\||k|\|><rsup|2>+m<rsup|2>|)><rsup|\<pm\>1>>),
    and <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|C|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2>\<to\>L<rsup|2>>\<leq\>m<rsup|-2>>.

    <\definition*>
      The <strong|Gaussian free field> <math|\<mu\><rsub|m>> is the centred
      Gaussian measure on <math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around|(|\<cal-M\>|)>>
      with

      <\equation*>
        <big|int>\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>*\<varphi\><around|(|g|)>*<space|0.17em>\<mu\><rsub|m><around|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>=<around|\<langle\>|f,C*g|\<rangle\>>,<space|2em><text|i.e.><space|2em><big|int>\<mathe\><rsup|\<mathi\>\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>>\<mu\><rsub|m><around|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>=\<mathe\><rsup|-<frac|1|2>*<around|\<langle\>|f,C*f|\<rangle\>>>.
      </equation*>
    </definition*>

    Formally <math|\<mu\><rsub|m><around|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>*`*`="*Z<rsup|-1>\<mathe\><rsup|-<frac|1|2>*<around|\<langle\>|\<varphi\>,A*\<varphi\>|\<rangle\>>>\<cal-D\>*\<varphi\>>:
    the Gaussian part of the Euclidean action.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The Green function>

    \;

    <wide-tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-lsep|0em>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-rsep|1em>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-width|0.58par>|<cwith|1|1|1|1|cell-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-width|0.38par>|<cwith|1|1|2|2|cell-hmode|exact>|<table|<row|<\cell>
      <math|C> has kernel <math|G>:

      <\equation*>
        G<rsub|m><around|(|x|)>=<big|int><frac|\<mathe\><rsup|\<mathi\>k\<cdot\>x>|<around|\||k|\|><rsup|2>+m<rsup|2>>*<frac|\<mathd\>k|<around|(|2*\<pi\>|)><rsup|d>>
      </equation*>

      on <math|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>>, and <math|<big|sum><rsub|n\<in\>\<bbb-Z\><rsup|d>>G<rsub|m>*<around|(|x+n*L|)>>
      on <math|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|L>>.

      <\itemize>
        <item><math|d=1>: <math|G<rsub|m><around|(|x|)>=\<mathe\><rsup|-m<around|\||x|\|>>/<around|(|2*m|)>>.

        <item><math|d=2>: <math|G<rsub|m><around|(|x|)>\<sim\><frac|1|2*\<pi\>>*log
        <frac|1|<around|\||x|\|>>>.

        <item><math|d\<geq\>3>: <math|G<rsub|m><around|(|x|)>\<sim\><frac|\<Gamma\>*<around|(|d/2-1|)>|4*\<pi\><rsup|d/2>><around|\||x|\|><rsup|2-d>>.

        <item>Decay <math|\<approx\>\<mathe\><rsup|-m<around|\||x|\|>>> at
        infinity.
      </itemize>

      <strong|Singular on the diagonal for <math|d\<geq\>2>>: the field is
      not a function.
    </cell>|<\cell>
      <image|<tuple|<#>|gff2d.png>|0.350par|||><next-line><vspace*|2pt>
      A sample of the massive GFF on <math|\<bbb-T\><rsup|2>> (<math|m=4>,
      <math|512<rsup|2>> Fourier modes).
    </cell>>>>>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Existence on the torus>

    \;

    <\theorem*>
      Let <math|<around|(|e<rsub|n>|)>> be a real orthonormal basis of
      eigenfunctions of <math|-\<Delta\>> on
      <math|\<bbb-T\><rsup|d><rsub|L>>, <math|-\<Delta\>*e<rsub|n>=\<kappa\><rsub|n>*e<rsub|n>>,
      <math|\<lambda\><rsub|n>=m<rsup|2>+\<kappa\><rsub|n>>, and
      <math|<around|(|g<rsub|n>|)>> i.i.d. <math|N<around|(|0,1|)>>. For
      <math|s\<gtr\><frac|d|2>-1>,

      <\equation*>
        \<varphi\>=<big|sum><rsub|n>\<lambda\><rsub|n><rsup|-1/2>*g<rsub|n>*<space|0.17em>e<rsub|n>
      </equation*>

      converges a.s. and in <math|L<rsup|2><around|(|\<bbb-P\>;H<rsup|-s>|)>>,
      and <math|<math-up|Law><around|(|\<varphi\>|)>=\<mu\><rsub|m>>.
    </theorem*>

    <with|font-series|bold|Proof.>

    <\equation*>
      \<bbb-E\><around|\<\|\|\>|\<varphi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2><rsub|H<rsup|-s>>=<big|sum><rsub|n><frac|1|<around|(|1+\<kappa\><rsub|n>|)><rsup|s>*\<lambda\><rsub|n>>\<asymp\><big|sum><rsub|k\<in\>\<bbb-Z\><rsup|d>><around|(|1+<around|\||k|\|><rsup|2>|)><rsup|-s-1>\<less\>\<infty\>\<Longleftrightarrow\>2*s+2\<gtr\>d.
    </equation*>

    <math|L<rsup|2>>-bounded <math|H<rsup|-s>>-valued martingale
    <math|\<Rightarrow\>> convergence. And
    <math|\<varphi\><around|(|f|)>=<big|sum><rsub|n>\<lambda\><rsub|n><rsup|-1/2>*g<rsub|n>*<around|\<langle\>|e<rsub|n>,f|\<rangle\>>>
    is Gaussian with variance <math|<big|sum><rsub|n>\<lambda\><rsub|n><rsup|-1>*<around|\<langle\>|e<rsub|n>,f|\<rangle\>><rsup|2>=<around|\<langle\>|f,C*f|\<rangle\>>>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Existence on <math|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>> and regularity>

    \;

    <\myframed>
      <strong|Bochner\UMinlos>

      <math|\<Psi\>:\<cal-S\><around|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>|)>\<to\>\<bbb-C\>>
      continuous, positive definite, <math|\<Psi\><around|(|0|)>=1>
      <math|\<Rightarrow\>> there is a unique probability measure on
      <math|\<cal-S\><rprime|'><around|(|\<bbb-R\><rsup|d>|)>> with
      characteristic functional <math|\<Psi\>>.
    </myframed>

    For <math|\<Psi\><around|(|f|)>=\<mathe\><rsup|-<frac|1|2>*<around|\<langle\>|f,C*f|\<rangle\>>>>:
    continuity from <math|<around|\<langle\>|f,C*f|\<rangle\>>\<leq\>m<rsup|-2><around|\<\|\|\>|f|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2>><rsup|2>>;
    positive definiteness from <math|\<Psi\>*<around|(|f<rsub|j>-f<rsub|k>|)>=a<rsub|j>*a<rsub|k>\<mathe\><rsup|<around|\<langle\>|f<rsub|j>,C*f<rsub|k>|\<rangle\>>>>
    and the Schur product theorem.

    <with|font-series|bold|Regularity> (sharp, Exercise 3.3):

    <tabular*|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-valign|c>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-tborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|2|2|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<table|<row|<cell|<math|d=1>>|<cell|<math|d=2>>|<cell|<math|d=3>>>|<row|<cell|stationary
    OU process>|<cell|<math|H<rsup|-\<kappa\>>>,
    <math|\<forall\>\<kappa\>\<gtr\>0>; not a
    function>|<cell|<math|H<rsup|-1/2-\<kappa\>>>>>>>>

    The Cameron\UMartin space <math|H<rsup|1>> (finite action) has
    <strong|measure zero>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
